## Vercel Speed Insights Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for this React/Vite application.

### Changes Made:

**Created:**
- None (only modifications to existing files)

**Modified:**
1. `package.json` - Added `@vercel/speed-insights` dependency (version ^1.0.14)
2. `package-lock.json` - Updated to reflect the new dependency installation
3. `src/App.jsx` - Added SpeedInsights component integration

### Implementation Details:

Following the official Vercel Speed Insights quickstart documentation (https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart), I:

1. **Installed the package**: Added `@vercel/speed-insights` using npm, which is the project's package manager.

2. **Integrated the component**: 
   - Imported `SpeedInsights` from `@vercel/speed-insights/react` (React-specific import for Vite projects)
   - Added the `<SpeedInsights />` component at the root level of the App component, just before the closing `</div>` tag
   - Positioned it outside the `<Suspense>` boundary to ensure it loads regardless of route changes

3. **Verified the implementation**:
   - Ran `npm run lint` - No new errors introduced (existing warnings are pre-existing)
   - Ran `npm run build` - Build completed successfully
   - All build artifacts (dist/) remain properly ignored by git

### Technical Notes:

- The SpeedInsights component is lightweight and will only track performance metrics when deployed to Vercel
- It automatically monitors Core Web Vitals (LCP, FID, CLS) and other performance metrics
- No additional configuration is required - it works out of the box
- The tracking script will be automatically deployed at `/_vercel/speed-insights/*` routes when the app is deployed to Vercel

### Verification:

To see Speed Insights data after deployment:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Wait for users to visit your site (or test it yourself)
3. View metrics in your Vercel dashboard under Speed Insights

The implementation follows React best practices and maintains the existing code structure without breaking any functionality.
